  "note": "Untuned v1 ranges. These are starting brackets, deliberately wide. Narrow them with `npm run narrow` against real ratings; do not hand-guess them. master.driveRmsDb is the loudness control and the first thing worth tuning by ear: the mix is trimmed to that RMS before the master chain, so it decides how hard the clipper works and therefore whether the transients still punch. bass.bias is deliberately near zero: asymmetric shaping on a 40 Hz sub produces DC that a blocker cannot remove without eating the fundamental, so even harmonics on the 808 come from drive and fold instead.",
